{"name":"Neon Romance","hex":"#e9023a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"neon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The chemical element (symbol Ne) with an atomic number of 10. The second of the noble gases, it is a colourless, odorless inert gas.\n A form or sample of the element.","A form or sample of the element."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That resembles a neon light; extremely bright; fluorescent"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neon"},{"term":"romance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An intimate relationship between two people; a love affair.","A strong obsession or attachment for something or someone."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To woo; to court.","To write or tell romantic stories, poetry, letters, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/romance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Neon","blocks":[{"text":"Neon is a chemical element; it has the symbol Ne and the atomic number 10. It is the second noble gas in the periodic table. Neon is a colorless, odorless, inert monatomic gas under standard conditions, with approximately two-thirds the density of air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Neon_discharge_tube.jpg/330px-Neon_discharge_tube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neon","wikidata":"Q654"},{"title":"Romance","blocks":[{"text":"Romance and romantic love encompass a number of ideas about love, which are interrelated for historical and cultural reasons:"},{"items":["passionate feelings of attraction—a mental state of \"being in love\", with focused attention (salience) towards a specific individual for courtship or pair bonding;","the cultural practice or idealization of initiating intimate relationships for feelings like these, over more practical or ordinary concerns;","a relationship or love affair initiated or maintained this way, which may be premarital or absent a commitment; and","a love story involving these elements."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg/330px-Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romance","wikidata":"Q1189047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/NeTube.jpg/500px-NeTube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/NeTube.jpg/1280px-NeTube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/NeTube.jpg/500px-NeTube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Neon gas-discharge lamps forming neon's element symbol","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANeTube.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG/500px-Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG/1280px-Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG/500px-Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The first evidence for isotopes of a stable element was provided in 1913 by experiments on neon plasma. In the bottom right corner of J. J. Thomson's photographic plate are the separate impact marks for the two isotopes neon-20 and neon-22.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiscovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg/500px-Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg/1280px-Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg/500px-Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The emission spectrum of neon shows individual wavelengths of light contributing to its perceived color when heated.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVisible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Ne-water_clathrate.png/500px-Ne-water_clathrate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Ne-water_clathrate.png/500px-Ne-water_clathrate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crystal structure of Ne clathrate hydrate[38]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANe-water_clathrate.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/FLORIST_%28neon_sign%29.jpg/500px-FLORIST_%28neon_sign%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/FLORIST_%28neon_sign%29.jpg/1280px-FLORIST_%28neon_sign%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/FLORIST_%28neon_sign%29.jpg/500px-FLORIST_%28neon_sign%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Neon sign in a Hamden, Connecticut, florist shop","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFLORIST_(neon_sign).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png/500px-Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png/500px-Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dopamine is produced in the ventral tegmental area (VTA) of the brain, and projected to the nucleus accumbens (NAc). Dopamine activity in the NAc is key to the attribution of salience.[84]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg/500px-Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg/1280px-Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg/500px-Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Crystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg/500px-Crystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Crystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg/1280px-Crystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Crystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg/500px-Crystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Crystallization\" was coined by the 19th-century French writer Stendhal to refer to the tendency of a person in love to overemphasize the positive aspects of their loved one and overlook the negative (\"love is blind\").[121][122][123][5] This idealization is now considered positive illusions, and significant scientific evidence has shown that it contributes to relationship satisfaction, long-term well-being and decreased risk for relationship discontinuation.[122][124]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg"}],"sounds":{"neon":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/47/En-us-neon.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/47/En-us-neon.ogg/En-us-neon.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Tesco250-neon.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/64/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Tesco250-neon.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Tesco250-neon.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/64/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Tesco250-neon.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Tesco250-neon.wav.ogg"}],"romance":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ec/En-us-romance.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ec/En-us-romance.ogg/En-us-romance.ogg.mp3"}]}}}